        { "id": "prt_02c", "sessionID": "ses_07", "messageID": "msg_02", "type": "text", "text": "It won't reject anything, unfortunately. TypeScript types are erased during compilation - by the time this code runs, `CreateTopicBody` doesn't exist anymore, and `req.body as CreateTopicBody` is just telling the compiler to trust you, it does no checking at runtime. If a client POSTs `{}`, `body.title` will just be `undefined` and `Topics.create` runs with bad data instead of failing loudly." },
