        { "id": "prt_04b", "sessionID": "ses_07", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "reasoning", "text": "Need to separate what TS guarantees (compile-time, within your own code) from what it can never guarantee (shape of data crossing a network boundary).", "time": { "start": 1758730026000, "end": 1758730027000 } },
        { "id": "prt_04c", "sessionID": "ses_07", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "text", "text": "TypeScript's value is catching mistakes *you* make while writing code - passing a string where a function expects a number, forgetting a field, etc - all caught by `tsc` before you ever run the app. But it has no way to check data that comes from outside your program, like an HTTP request body, because that data doesn't exist yet when the compiler runs. `as CreateTopicBody` is a type assertion, not a check - it just silences the compiler. For request bodies you need an actual runtime check: either hand-written (`typeof body.title === 'string'`) or a validation library like zod that both validates and gives you the type." },
        { "id": "prt_04d", "sessionID": "ses_07", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "stop", "cost": 0.025, "tokens": { "input": 1700, "output": 460, "reasoning": 0, "cache": { "read": 0, "write": 0 } } }
